## Error Handling

### ACP Errors Through MAP

ACP errors are passed through unchanged:

```typescript
// ACP error in MAP response payload
{
  payload: {
    acp: {
      jsonrpc: '2.0',
      id: originalRequestId,
      error: {
        code: -32000,  // ACP error code preserved
        message: 'Authentication required',
        data: { ... }
      }
    },
    acpContext: { streamId, sessionId, direction: 'agent-to-client' }
  }
}

// Client receives as ACPError
class ACPError extends Error {
  constructor(public code: number, message: string, public data?: unknown);
}

try {
  await acp.newSession({...});
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof ACPError && e.code === -32000) {
    // Handle ACP auth_required
  }
}
```

### Error Scenarios

| Scenario | Handling |
|----------|----------|
| Target agent unavailable | ACPStreamConnection throws with agent unavailable error |
| MAP message timeout | ACPStreamConnection throws with timeout error |
| Agent returns ACP error | ACPError propagated to caller unchanged |
| Client disconnects during agent request | Agent receives disconnect, should abort |
| Stream closed during operation | Pending operations reject with stream closed error |
| Session lost after reconnection | `sessionLost` event emitted, client can use `loadSession` |

