## SDK Integration Options

### Option A: Raw Protocol (Zero SDK Changes)

Mail works today with no SDK changes. Agents use the generic `sendRequest()` method:

```typescript
// Works with current BaseConnection
await connection.sendRequest('mail/create', { type: 'multi-agent', subject: '...' });
await connection.sendRequest('mail/turn', { conversationId: '...', contentType: 'text', content: { text: '...' } });
```

This is a valid approach for early adoption and testing.

### Option B: Typed MailClient (Recommended)

A standalone class that wraps BaseConnection with typed methods:

```typescript
import { BaseConnection } from '@multi-agent-protocol/sdk';

class MailClient {
  #connection: BaseConnection;

  constructor(connection: BaseConnection) {
    this.#connection = connection;
  }

  get enabled(): boolean {
    return !!this.#connection.serverCapabilities?.mail?.enabled;
  }

  async create(params: MailCreateRequest): Promise<MailCreateResponse> {
    return this.#connection.sendRequest('mail/create', params);
  }

  async get(params: MailGetRequest): Promise<MailGetResponse> {
    return this.#connection.sendRequest('mail/get', params);
  }

  async turn(params: MailTurnRequest): Promise<MailTurnResponse> {
    return this.#connection.sendRequest('mail/turn', params);
  }

  async listTurns(params: MailTurnsListRequest): Promise<MailTurnsListResponse> {
    return this.#connection.sendRequest('mail/turns/list', params);
  }

  async close(params: MailCloseRequest): Promise<MailCloseResponse> {
    return this.#connection.sendRequest('mail/close', params);
  }

  // ... other methods
}

// Usage
const agent = new AgentConnection(stream);
await agent.connect({ agentId: 'orchestrator' });

const mail = new MailClient(agent.connection);
if (mail.enabled) {
  const conv = await mail.create({ type: 'multi-agent', subject: 'Sprint planning' });
}
```

### Option C: Convenience Methods on AgentConnection

Sugar methods that make mail-aware sending ergonomic:

```typescript
// On AgentConnection
async sendInConversation(
  conversationId: ConversationId,
  to: Address,
  payload?: unknown,
  meta?: MessageMeta
): Promise<SendResponseResult> {
  return this.send(to, payload, {
    ...meta,
    mail: { conversationId, ...meta?.mail }
  });
}

async replyInConversation(
  originalMessage: Message,
  payload?: unknown,
  meta?: MessageMeta
): Promise<SendResponseResult> {
  return this.reply(originalMessage, payload, {
    ...meta,
    mail: originalMessage.meta?.mail
  });
}
```

