## Pattern: Mail Context Propagation

For multi-hop agent chains (A → B → C), the mail context should propagate:

```typescript
// Agent B receives from A, delegates to C
agent.onMessage(async (message) => {
  const mailCtx = message.meta?.mail;

  // Delegate subtask to Agent C, preserving mail context
  await agent.send(
    { agent: 'agent-c' },
    { subtask: 'validate', data: message.payload },
    { mail: mailCtx }
  );
});

// Agent C receives from B, replies
agent.onMessage(async (message) => {
  const result = await validate(message.payload.data);

  // Reply preserving mail context
  await agent.reply(message, { valid: true }, {
    mail: message.meta?.mail
  });
});
```

All three hops (A→B, B→C, C→B) are recorded as turns in the same conversation because each agent forwarded the `mail` meta.

