## Pattern: Trajectory Child Conversations

When an orchestrator wants to track an agent's internal work separately from the main conversation:

```typescript
// Orchestrator creates main conversation
const mainConv = await mail.create({ 
  type: 'user-session', 
  subject: 'User request' 
});

// Create child conversation for agent trajectory
const trajectory = await mail.create({
  type: 'agent-task',
  subject: 'researcher work log',
  parentConversationId: mainConv.conversation.id,
});

// Send task to researcher with BOTH conversation IDs
await orchestrator.send(
  { agent: 'researcher' },
  { 
    task: 'research', 
    query: '...',
    trajectoryConversationId: trajectory.conversation.id  // in payload, not meta
  },
  { mail: { conversationId: mainConv.conversation.id } }  // main conversation in meta
);
```

The researcher can then record tool calls in the trajectory conversation:

```typescript
agent.onMessage(async (message) => {
  const mainConvId = message.meta?.mail?.conversationId;
  const trajectoryConvId = message.payload.trajectoryConversationId;

  // Record tool call in trajectory (if provided)
  if (trajectoryConvId) {
    await agent.request('mail/turn', {
      conversationId: trajectoryConvId,
      contentType: 'x-tool-call',
      content: { tool: 'search', input: { query: '...' } }
    });
  }

  const results = await doResearch();

  // Reply to main conversation
  await agent.reply(message, { results }, {
    mail: { conversationId: mainConvId }
  });
});
```

